---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';

const { contact } = site;
---

<SiteLayout title="Privacy" description={`How ${site.legalName} uses the information you share through this website.`}>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Privacy" title="Privacy policy" breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} />

  <article class="container-site py-12 md:py-16">
    <div class="prose-article mx-auto max-w-[720px]">
      <p><strong>Last updated: 26 October 2026</strong></p>
      <p>
        This website is run by {site.legalName}, a not-for-profit school at {contact.address}. This policy explains what
        information we collect through the website, why we collect it and what we do with it. If you have any questions,
        email us at <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>We only collect what you choose to send us through the forms on this website:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Admission enquiries:</strong> the guardian's name, a phone number, the child's age, the area you live in and your message.</li>
        <li><strong>Volunteering:</strong> your name, email, phone number, what you would like to teach and which Saturdays you can commit to.</li>
        <li><strong>Contact form:</strong> your name, email, phone number (if you give one), the topic and your message.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You don't need an account to use this website, and we don't ask for any information just to browse it.</p>

      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <p>
        We use your information only to reply to you and to deal with your enquiry: to arrange an admission, plan a
        Saturday Scholars session or answer your question. We don't use it for marketing, and we never sell it or share it
        with anyone for their own use.
      </p>
      <p>
        Only the Al-Bayan staff who handle your enquiry can see it. It is stored with the service providers we use to run
        this website and our email, who keep it secure and may not use it for anything else.
      </p>
      <p>
        We keep your information only for as long as we need it to deal with your enquiry, and then delete it. If your
        child joins the school or you start volunteering with us, we keep the details we need for that.
      </p>

      <h2>Photos of children</h2>
      <p>
        We only show a child in a photo on this website with their parent or guardian's consent. We never name children
        in photos. If you would like a photo removed, email us at <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>
        and we will take it down.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>This website does not use cookies, and it has no advertising or tracking.</p>
      <p>
        The map on our Contact page comes from Google Maps. It loads only if you press "Show the map", and Google may then
        set its own cookies. Links to Instagram, Facebook, LinkedIn and WhatsApp take you to those services, which have
        their own privacy policies.
      </p>
      <p>
        Like any website, the service that hosts this site (Cloudflare) keeps short-term technical records of visits, such
        as your IP address, to keep the site secure and working.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask us what information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it. Email
        <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a> and we will reply as soon as we can.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>If we change how we use your information, we will update this page and the date at the top.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
